@@ -0,0 +1,125 @@
+# Community-Contributed Hidden Gems Discovery Platform
+
+Resolves #865 — Implement Community-Contributed Hidden Gems Discovery
+Platform with AI-Based Quality Ranking.
+
+Extends the existing static `frontend/hidden-gems/hidden-gems.html` page
+(previously 8 hardcoded destinations with an inline script) into a
+community contribution platform: travelers can submit hidden gems,
+submissions get an automated content-quality score and duplicate check,
+a moderator reviews them, approved gems are ranked and surfaced in a
+trending section, and contributors build reputation and badges.
+
+Like the rest of this project, it's entirely client-side — no backend,
+no database, no API keys.
+
+## Files added / changed
+
+| File | Purpose |
+| ---- | ------- |
+| `js-modules/hidden-gems-data.js` | Config: categories, regions, moderation statuses, quality-scoring weights, banned/placeholder word lists, reputation events, badge tiers, ranking weights, duplicate thresholds, and the original 8 destinations re-modeled as pre-approved "editorial" seed gems. |
+| `js-modules/hidden-gems-core.js` | Pure logic: text-similarity duplicate detection, content-quality scoring, ranking/trending score, reputation & badges, moderation status transitions. No DOM, no fetch — unit-testable. |
+| `js-modules/hidden-gems-service.js` | `localStorage`-backed persistence: submissions, contributor reputation, votes, bookmarks, reports, moderator-mode toggle. |
+| `js-modules/hidden-gems-ui.js` | DOM layer (`initHiddenGemsPage`): grid rendering, search/filter, submission form, moderation dashboard, trending section, leaderboard, upvote/bookmark/report actions. |
+| `frontend/hidden-gems/hidden-gems.html` (modified) | Added submission form, trending section, moderator-mode toggle + dashboard, and contributor leaderboard markup. Removed the old inline `<script>` — logic now lives in the modules above. |
+| `frontend/hidden-gems/hidden-gems-community.css` | Styles for the new sections, reusing the page's existing design tokens. |
+| `tests/unit/hidden-gems-core.test.js` | Unit tests for scoring, duplicate detection, ranking, reputation, and moderation transitions. |
+| `js-modules/router-init.js` (modified) | `hidden-gems.html` now loads the four modules above and calls `initHiddenGemsPage()`, replacing the previous `log`-only entry. |
+
+## Why "AI-assisted" means a transparent heuristic here, not a model
+
+The issue asks for "AI-based duplicate detection" and "AI-generated
+content quality scoring." This repo has no backend and no way to call a
+trained model, so both are implemented as **deterministic, documented
+heuristics** — not machine learning:
+
+- **Duplicate detection** (`detectDuplicates` in `hidden-gems-core.js`):
+  Jaccard similarity (shared words ÷ total distinct words, stopwords
+  removed) between a new submission's name+description and every
+  existing gem's, combined with a straight-line distance check when both
+  have coordinates. A match on name, high text similarity (≥ 0.6), or
+  close text + close coordinates flags the pair.
+- **Content-quality scoring** (`computeQualityScore`): a weighted rubric
+  out of 100 — description length (30), has an image (15), has precise
+  coordinates (15), has a category (10), title looks reasonable (10),
+  and doesn't contain banned/placeholder text (20).
+
+Neither one auto-publishes or auto-deletes anything — they only produce
+a score and a list of flags that a human moderator sees before deciding.
+This is called out in code comments in `hidden-gems-core.js` as well, so
+it's clear to future contributors and isn't just a UI label.
+
+## Submission → moderation → publish flow
+
+1. A visitor fills out the submission form (name, description, category,
+   region, optional state/coordinates/photo URL, and a display name).
+2. `HiddenGemsService.submitGem()` runs `computeQualityScore()` and
+   `detectDuplicates()` against every existing gem (seed + community),
+   stores the submission with `status: 'pending'`, and shows the
+   contributor their score, any quality flags, and any duplicate
+   warning immediately.
+3. A moderator (see below) reviews the pending queue and can **Approve**,
+   **Reject**, or **Request Changes** — enforced by
+   `transitionStatus()`'s `VALID_TRANSITIONS` table, e.g. a rejected
+   submission can be resubmitted (`rejected -> pending`) but an approved
+   one can't jump straight back to pending.
+4. On approval, the gem appears in the public grid and trending section;
+   the contributor's reputation increases
+   (`REPUTATION_EVENTS.SUBMISSION_APPROVED`, +15).
+
+## Ranking / trending
+
+`computeRankScore()` combines:
+
+- **Quality component**: `qualityScore × 0.5`
+- **Engagement component**: `(upvotes × 3 + bookmarks × 1)`, multiplied
+  by a recency factor that halves every 21 days
+  (`RANKING_WEIGHTS.recencyHalfLifeDays`) since `approvedAt` — so an old
+  gem with a lot of historical upvotes doesn't permanently outrank
+  something newer and currently popular.
+
+`trendingGems()` filters to `status: 'approved'` and returns the top N
+by rank score.
+
+## Reputation & badges
+
+Every contributor is identified by the display name they type into the
+submission form (see limitations below). `REPUTATION_EVENTS` in
+`hidden-gems-data.js` defines the point values:
+
+| Event | Points |
+| ----- | ------ |
+| Submission approved | +15 |
+| Submission rejected | −3 |
+| Gem receives an upvote | +1 |
+| A report against your gem is upheld | −10 |
+
+Reputation maps to a badge tier (`badgeForReputation()`): Newcomer (0) →
+Explorer (20) → Pathfinder (60) → Trailblazer (150) → Local Legend (400).
+
+## Known limitations / follow-ups
+
+- **No real backend.** Submissions, votes, bookmarks, reports, and
+  reputation all live in `localStorage`, scoped to one browser. They
+  don't sync across devices or between different contributors' browsers
+  — the "community" aspect is a working local simulation of the intended
+  workflow, ready to swap onto a real API (`submitGem` /
+  `moderateSubmission` / `toggleUpvote` are already isolated in
+  `hidden-gems-service.js` as the seam to do that).
+- **Contributor identity is just a typed display name**, not an account.
+  Two people could type the same name and share a reputation record.
+  Wiring this to the site's existing optional Firebase login
+  (`auth.js`) would fix this and is a natural next step.
+- **Moderator Mode is a local toggle**, not a real permission check —
+  anyone can click "🛡️ Moderator Mode" to see the dashboard. This is
+  a stand-in until the project has server-verified roles (Firebase
+  custom claims + a Cloud Function, following the pattern hinted at by
+  `auth.js`'s existing `role` claim for premium users).
+- **Image upload isn't implemented** — contributors paste a photo URL
+  rather than uploading a file. Real file storage needs a backend
+  (or a third-party bucket + signed upload URLs); a client-only site
+  can't safely host arbitrary user-uploaded images.
+- **Quality/duplicate detection is a heuristic, not a trained model** —
+  see the section above. It's intentionally simple and transparent so
+  false positives/negatives are easy to reason about and tune via the
+  weights in `hidden-gems-data.js`.
